  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>doxycycline</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>J01AA02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Toutain PL et al. 2025</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>pigs</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>doxycycline</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>accepted with caveats</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_doxycycline/Doxycycline_Toutain2025_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Vc</td><td>0.192</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>V2</td><td>0.595</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr><tr><td>V3</td><td>0.536</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>V3</small></td></tr><tr><td>Clearance</td><td>0.259</td><td>L/kg/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>Cld2</td><td>1.179</td><td>L/kg/h</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr><tr><td>MAT_FEED_TLS</td><td>13.89</td><td>h</td><td><small>MAT</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_q88_category</td><td>38.6</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr></table><h4>About doxycycline</h4><p>Doxycycline is a tetracycline antibiotic used to treat many bacterial infections, including pneumonia, acne, Lyme disease, and chlamydia, and to prevent malaria. It is widely used in human medicine and is also approved for veterinary use, and it appears on the WHO list of essential medicines.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422442\">Wikidata Q422442</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Doxycycline\">Doxycycline</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Toutain PL et al. (2025). Pharmacokinetic-Pharmacodynamic Cutoff Values for Doxycycline in Pigs to Support the Establishment of Clinical Breakpoints for Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing. <i>Journal of veterinary pharmacology and therapeutics 48(4):300–317</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/jvp.13511\">10.1111/jvp.13511</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40247665\">40247665</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Toutain_2025: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"),
